export const SEARCH_MODELS_DESCRIPTION = "Search the live VideoClaw model catalog with a model name or a plain purpose (for example \"nano banana 2\" or \"upscale a video\"), or leave query empty to browse. kind narrows the output (image, video or audio); inputs keeps only models that accept every listed input kind. Each model appears once under an opaque model_id; use it exactly as returned, never edit or compose one, and never pick a provider yourself. Browse pages give short metadata that may be unverified: a null output_type, supported_inputs or callable, or availability=unverified, means not checked yet, not unsupported (supported_inputs=null is unknown, not none). If inputs_complete is false or absent, supported_inputs lists only proven kinds; inspect the exact ID's input_schema before ruling out other inputs. kind and inputs leave out models whose output or inputs are not known yet (omitted_unknown counts them), so a filtered page is not a complete list of every capable model; if omitted_unknown>0, narrow the purpose with fewer input filters, then inspect exact IDs' schemas. For one model's current details (callable, input_schema, price), search with its exact model_id as query. partial=true means this page is incomplete; has_more=true means more results exist, read them by passing next_cursor as cursor with the same query, kind and inputs; if a cursor is refused, search again with the same query, kind and inputs and no cursor. total appears only when the count is complete. Choose a result with callable=true and call_model with that model_id and an input that satisfies its exact input_schema, including required price dimensions such as duration or resolution. Prefer a suitable result with usable pre-run pricing. pricing.kind=unknown-cost and pricing_note mark models without a usable estimate; use them only when no priceable result satisfies the brief. Missing pricing on an unverified result means inspect its exact model_id first, not that it is unpriceable. callable=false with retryable=true means the model is fine but its price or account check is briefly unavailable; the app already waited up to two minutes, so do other useful work and search again after retry_after_s instead of searching other names. callable=false without retryable names a real limit in unavailable_reason (for example no numeric provider price). catalog_status=PROVIDER_CREDENTIAL_MISCONFIGURED means VideoClaw's own provider key was refused: tell the user catalog_message; the models it names are not at fault, and waiting or searching again will not fix it. For stock/default generation, use the existing mint_image, mint_video, synth_voice or music tools without requiring catalog search; a failed search does not establish that those tools are unavailable, so submit the intended operation and respect its actual authorization/provider result. Keep explicitly requested models exact; never silently substitute a default for an unavailable requested model.";
